-- LRA/NumberSystems/IntegerStructure/Bundled.lean
-- A self-contained (non-`Element`/`SetObject`-generic) presentation of the
-- two-sided successor/predecessor axioms, with categoricity proved
-- concretely against Lean's built-in `Int`.

namespace LRA.NumberSystems.IntegerStructure.Bundled

/-!
Volume II label: integers-polish-discrete-integer-structure
Verification status: experimental statement/proof work

This module formalizes the abstract `(Z1)`--`(Z3)` integer-structure axioms:

* successor and predecessor are mutual inverses,
* positive successor iterates of zero are aperiodic,
* two-sided induction holds.

The intended theorem is categoricity: every such structure is represented by
the built-in `Int` through the unique walk generated by `succ` and `pred`.

Moved from `LRA.VolumeII.Integers.Polish.DiscreteIntegerStructure` (no
change to its proofs). This module bundles its carrier as a plain field
(`carrier : Type u`) rather than taking `Element`/`SetObject` as external
parameters, so it sits alongside -- not inside -- the `Element`/`SetObject`-
generic presentation in `IntegerStructure.Definition`/`.Categoricity`, the
way `NModel` sits alongside `PeanoSystem.PeanoSystem`: a second, self-
contained presentation of the same idea, proved here concretely against
`Int` rather than model-to-model. Unifying the two is tracked in
`Integers/ProofOrder.md`.
-/

